Ignore deployer.conf in check-config.sh.

deployer.conf is the configuration file of a containerised deployer
launcher, kept beside globals.yml in the deploy host's configuration
directory and owned by the deploy user. Skip it when check-config.sh
checks file permissions and ownership.

Like globals.yml, passwords.yml and kolla-build.conf, which are already
skipped, it is not service configuration written by kolla-ansible.

